<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 78,263 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 78,263 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 78,263 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7.00 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 56,009 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>						Wednesday   September 17</p>
<p>    Export cargo			  10,784	4,845</p>
<p>    Import cargo			  67,479     51,164</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and three berthed. In the next 24 hours, five were expected to sail and 12 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		  56,000	 Keefan		 19/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		  8,000	 Strength	     21/9</p>
<p>Palm oil		 13,000	 Bunga Anggarik     23/9</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
